The build failed with 'fg: no job control' error in the %build section when executing %py3_wheel. This is a shell/job control issue, not a missing dependency. The spec uses %py3_wheel and %py3_install which are correct for Python 3 builds. The BuildRequires include %{python_module pip} and %{python_module hatchling} which are fine. The spec has python-rpm-macros which is needed for %{python_module}. The actual issue is that the %py3_wheel macro expansion is causing a job control problem - likely because the macro expansion is trying to spawn a background process. The fix is to use %pyproject_wheel and %pyproject_install macros instead, as the project uses pyproject.toml. Looking at the initial spec review, it mentions the spec should use %pyproject_wheel and %pyproject_install instead of %py3_wheel and %py3_install. The correct macros for pyproject.toml projects are %pyproject_wheel and %pyproject_install. Let me update the %build and %install sections to use these macros.